arks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/tp3_cd3_ext.cpp\n\ndiff --git a/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/README.md b/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/README.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..417e12f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/README.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@\n+# TilePalette3 and ChunkDelta3: GH200 handoff\n+\n+This directory contains only the two accepted lossless BF16 formats. It does\n+not include any rejected intermediate variants.\n+\n+- **TilePalette3 (TP3):** one Top-7 exponent palette per 64x64 tile, 3-bit\n+  codes, and packed 17-bit `(exponent8, warp_position9)` exceptions.\n+- **ChunkDelta3 (CD3):** one exponent base per 16-value thread chunk, 3-bit\n+  deltas, and the same packed 17-bit exception stream.\n+\n+Both compressors and decompressors are self-contained. They accept contiguous\n+2-D BF16 tensors whose dimensions are multiples of 64 and reconstruct all\n+65,536 BF16 bit patterns exactly.\n+\n+## Build on GH200\n+\n+```bash\n+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python build_extension.py --arch sm_90a\n+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python smoke_test.py\n+```\n+\n+The build prints ptxas register, spill, and shared-memory information. Record\n+that output with the result; the B200 build used 40 registers/thread for TP3\n+and 37 registers/thread for CD3, but GH200 must be measured independently.\n+\n+## Benchmark an actual weight\n+\n+Save one contiguous two-dimensional weight tensor as a `.pt` file, then run:\n+\n+```bash\n+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python benchmark_frozen_split.py \\\n+  --input /path/to/weight.pt \\\n+  --output gh200_tp3_cd3_weight.json\n+```\n+\n+For a state dictionary, also pass `--key model.layers.39.self_attn.q_proj.weight`\n+or the relevant key. The benchmark reports resident decode, H2D-only, and\n+sequential H2D+decode separately. It uses the intended frozen-split placement:\n+\n+| Codec | Permanently HBM-resident | Transferred from Grace LPDDR |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| TP3 | sign/mantissa, palette, tile offsets, warp prefixes | codes, entries17 |\n+| CD3 | sign/mantissa, tile offsets, warp prefixes | codes, thread bases, entries17 |\n+\n+The sequential result is not a substitute for the real TieredServe overlapped\n+pipeline. After the component comparison, integrate both codecs behind the\n+same prefetch schedule and compare layer latency and end-to-end token latency.\n+\n+## Integration surface\n+\n+The Python-visible compressed objects expose exactly the payloads required by\n+`SplitStorageInfo`:\n+\n+- `CompressedTilePalette3`: `palettes8`, `codes`, `sign_mantissa`,\n+  `tile_exception_offsets`, `warp_prefixes`, `entries17`, `M`, `K`.\n+- `CompressedChunkDelta3`: `codes`, `sign_mantissa`, `thread_bases`,\n+  `tile_exception_offsets`, `warp_prefixes`, `entries17`, `M`, `K`.\n+\n+The CUDA decoders use no dynamic allocation, no shared memory, and no CTA-wide\n+barrier. TP3 keeps the final warp-local patch format; CD3 keeps the final\n+`__launch_bounds__(256, 6)` occupancy constraint.\n+\n+## Claim boundary\n+\n+The code is portable to Hopper, but B200 performance numbers are not GH200\n+results. A GH200 claim requires bit-exact validation plus representative KV and\n+weight measurements using the same compiler, clocks, placement, and pipeline\n+configuration for both codecs.\ndiff --git a/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/benchmark_frozen_split.py b/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/benchmark_frozen_split.py\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..d7d3d0b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/benchmark_frozen_split.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,248 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Measure resident decode and sequential frozen-split H2D + decode.\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import argparse\n+import hashlib\n+import importlib.util\n+import json\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from typing import Callable\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import torch\n+\n+\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n+\n+\n+def parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--input\", type=Path, required=True)\n+    parser.add_argument(\n+        \"--key\", help=\"state-dict key when --input contains a dictionary\"\n+    )\n+    parser.add_argument(\n+        \"--extension\", type=Path, default=ROOT / \"build/tp3_cd3_ext.so\"\n+    )\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--warmups\", type=int, default=20)\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--runs\", type=int, default=200)\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path)\n+    return parser.parse_args()\n+\n+\n+def load_extension(path: Path):\n+    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"tp3_cd3_ext\", path)\n+    if spec is None or spec.loader is None:\n+        raise RuntimeError(f\"cannot load extension: {path}\")\n+    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n+    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n+    return module\n+\n+\n+def load_source(path: Path, key: str | None) -> torch.Tensor:\n+    loaded = torch.load(path, map_location=\"cpu\", weights_only=True)\n+    if isinstance(loaded, torch.Tensor):\n+        tensor = loaded\n+    elif isinstance(loaded, dict):\n+        if key is None:\n+            raise ValueError(\"--key is required for a dictionary checkpoint\")\n+        tensor = loaded[key]\n+    else:\n+        raise TypeError(\"--input must contain a tensor or a tensor dictionary\")\n+    if tensor.dim() != 2:\n+        raise ValueError(f\"expected a 2-D tensor, got shape {tuple(tensor.shape)}\")\n+    if tensor.shape[0] % 64 or tensor.shape[1] % 64:\n+        raise ValueError(\"both tensor dimensions must be multiples of 64\")\n+    return tensor.to(torch.bfloat16).contiguous().cuda()\n+\n+\n+def sha256(path: Path) -> str:\n+    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n+    with path.open(\"rb\") as file:\n+        while chunk := file.read(1024 * 1024):\n+            digest.update(chunk)\n+    return digest.hexdigest()\n+\n+\n+def summarize(samples: list[float]) -> dict[str, float]:\n+    values = np.asarray(samples, dtype=np.float64)\n+    return {\n+        \"p50_ms\": float(np.percentile(values, 50)),\n+        \"p90_ms\": float(np.percentile(values, 90)),\n+        \"p99_ms\": float(np.percentile(values, 99)),\n+        \"mean_ms\": float(values.mean()),\n+        \"min_ms\": float(values.min()),\n+        \"max_ms\": float(values.max()),\n+    }\n+\n+\n+def time_call(call: Callable[[], object], warmups: int, runs: int) -> dict[str, float]:\n+    for _ in range(warmups):\n+        call()\n+    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n+    begin = torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True)\n+    end = torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True)\n+    samples: list[float] = []\n+    for _ in range(runs):\n+        begin.record()\n+        call()\n+        end.record()\n+        end.synchronize()\n+        samples.append(begin.elapsed_time(end))\n+    return summarize(samples)\n+\n+\n+def pinned_payload(compressed, attributes: tuple[str, ...]) -> dict[str, torch.Tensor]:\n+    return {\n+        name: getattr(compressed, name).detach().cpu().pin_memory()\n+        for name in attributes\n+    }\n+\n+\n+def copy_payload(\n+    host: dict[str, torch.Tensor],\n+    staged,\n+    attributes: tuple[str, ...],\n+) -> None:\n+    for name in attributes:\n+        getattr(staged, name).copy_(host[name], non_blocking=True)\n+\n+\n+def stage_tile_palette3(extension, compressed):\n+    staged = extension.CompressedTilePalette3()\n+    for name in (\n+        \"palettes8\",\n+        \"sign_mantissa\",\n+        \"tile_exception_offsets\",\n+        \"warp_prefixes\",\n+    ):\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a03d13-c3dd-7442-8121-0c22895b2ef0","create_time":1787731115.113519}}}
