ama-3.1-70B-Instruct'}\\nThe global random seed is set to 0. Since VLLM_ENABLE_V1_MULTIPROCESSING is set to False, this may affect the random state of the Python process that launched vLLM.\\nResolved architecture: LlamaForCausalLM\\nUsing max model len 8192\\nChunked prefill is enabled with max_num_batched_tokens=8192.\\nWe must use the `spawn` multiprocessing start method. Overriding VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD to 'spawn'. See https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/usage/troubleshooting.html#python-multiprocessing for more information. Reasons: CUDA is initialized\\nSupported tasks: ['generate']\\nDefault sampling parameters have been overridden by the model's Hugging Face generation config recommended from the model creator. If t…3543 tokens truncated…ered-serve runs them:\n\n    qkv     = cat(q_proj, k_proj, v_proj)   (e.g. 10240 x 8192)\n    o       = o_proj                        (e.g.  8192 x 8192)\n    gateup  = cat(gate_proj, up_proj)       (e.g. 57344 x 8192)\n    down    = down_proj                     (e.g.  8192 x 28672)\n\neach is then round-tripped through each selected tiered-serve weight codec\n(use ``--per-tensor`` to benchmark the raw, un-fused q/k/v/... weights instead):\n\n    p4flat     – P4FlatCompressor      (per-tile palette4, BF16)\n    ublb_flat  – UBLBFlatCompressor    (U4 flat, BF16, fused-MM)\n    ublb       – UBLBCompressor        (nvcomp gdeflate UB/LB split, BF16)\n    zipserv    – ZipServCompressor     (TCA-TBE triple bitmap, BF16)\n    dietgpu    – DietGPUCompressor     (ANS exponent codec, BF16)\n    dietgpu_fp8 / zipserv_fp8          (FP8 e4m3 weights)\n\nFor each (weight, codec) it reports the compression ratio, compress and\ndecompress latency (ms, best of N runs), the compress/decompress throughput\nover the original weight bytes (GiB/s, 1024^3), and a bit-exact round-trip\ncheck.  These codecs are lossless, so ``OK`` should always be ✓.\n\nRun from the tiered-serve repo root (PYTHONPATH not required — the script\nadds the repo root to sys.path itself):\n  python benchmarks/weight_compress.py meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct\n  python benchmarks/weight_compress.py <model-id> --layer 0\n  python benchmarks/weight_compress.py <model-id> --group qkv,down\n  python benchmarks/weight_compress.py <model-id> --codec p4flat,zipserv\n  python benchmarks/weight_compress.py <model-id> --per-tensor --key q_proj\n\nModelled on /root/projects/LLM-bitfield-compressor/scripts/compress_weights.py\nbut driven entirely through the production tiered-serve compressor classes.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport glob\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom collections import OrderedDict, defaultdict\n\n# Allow running as `python benchmarks/weight_compress.py ...` from the repo root\n# (or anywhere) without needing PYTHONPATH — add the repo root (parent of this\n# benchmarks/ dir) to sys.path so `import tiered_serve` resolves.\n_REPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\nif _REPO_ROOT not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, _REPO_ROOT)\n\n# Reduce fragmentation OOMs when the GPU is shared with another process (e.g. a\n# serving run); must be set before torch initialises CUDA.\nos.environ.setdefault(\"PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF\", \"expandable_segments:True\")\n\nimport torch\nfrom safetensors import safe_open\n\n\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n#  HuggingFace cache resolution  (model id -> safetensors shard paths)\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\ndef _hf_cache_roots():\n    \"\"\"Candidate HuggingFace hub cache directories, in priority order.\"\"\"\n    roots = []\n    for env in (\"HF_HUB_CACHE\", \"HUGGINGFACE_HUB_CACHE\"):\n        if os.environ.get(env):\n            roots.append(os.environ[env])\n    if os.environ.get(\"HF_HOME\"):\n        roots.append(os.path.join(os.environ[\"HF_HOME\"], \"hub\"))\n    roots.append(os.path.expanduser(\"~/.cache/huggingface/hub\"))\n    seen, uniq = set(), []\n    for r in roots:\n        r = os.path.abspath(r)\n        if r not in seen and os.path.isdir(r):\n            seen.add(r); uniq.append(r)\n    return uniq\n\n\ndef _resolve_hf_model(model_id):\n    \"\"\"Return safetensors paths for a HF model id (``org/name``) from the cache.\n\n    Picks the most recently modified snapshot that holds ``.safetensors`` files.\n    \"\"\"\n    if \"/\" not in model_id:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(\n            f\"Model id must look like 'org/name' (got {model_id!r})\")\n    org, name = model_id.split(\"/\", 1)\n    dir_name = f\"models--{org}--{name}\"\n    snapshots = []\n    for root in _hf_cache_roots():\n        snap_root = os.path.join(root, dir_name, \"snapshots\")\n        if os.path.isdir(snap_root):\n            snapshots += [os.path.join(snap_root, s) for s in os.listdir(snap_root)\n                          if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(snap_root, s))]\n    if not snapshots:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(\n            f\"No HF cache entry for {model_id!r}. Searched: \"\n            f\"{', '.join(_hf_cache_roots()) or '(none)'}\")\n    snapshots.sort(key=os.path.getmtime, reverse=True)\n    for snap in snapshots:\n        files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(snap, \"*.safetensors\")))\n        if files:\n            return files\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\n        f\"{model_id!r} is cached but has no .safetensors shards.\")\n\n\ndef _resolve_inputs(inputs):\n    \"\"\"Expand file paths and HF model ids into a flat list of shard paths.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for s in inputs:\n        if os.path.isfile(s) and s.endswith(\".safetensors\"):\n            out.append(s)\n        elif os.path.isfile(s):\n            sys.exit(f\"Unsupported file (need .safetensors): {s}\")\n        elif \"/\" in s and not os.path.exists(s):\n            try:\n                resolved = _resolve_hf_model(s)\n            except FileNotFoundError as e:\n                sys.exit(str(e))\n            print(f\"  Resolved HF model {s!r} -> {len(resolved)} shard(s) in \"\n                  f\"{os.path.dirname(resolved[0])}\")\n            out += resolved\n        else:\n            sys.exit(f\"Not found: {s}\")\n    return out\n\n\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n#  Weight-key filtering\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n_PROJ_NAMES = (\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"v_proj\", \"o_proj\",\n               \"gate_proj\", \"up_proj\", \"down_proj\",\n               \".wq.\", \".wk.\", \".wv.\", \".wo.\", \".w1.\", \".w2.\", \".w3.\")\n\n\ndef _filter_keys(keys, key, all_weights, layer, max_weights, already):\n    if key:\n        keys = [k for k in keys if key in k]\n    elif not all_weights:\n        keys = [k for k in keys if any(p in k for p in _PROJ_NAMES)]\n    if layer is not None:\n        keys = [k for k in keys if f\"layers.{layer}.\" in k]\n    if max_weights > 0:\n        keys = keys[:max(0, max_weights - already)]\n    return keys\n\n\ndef _short_name(name):\n    return (name.replace(\"model.layers.\", \"L\")\n                .replace(\".self_attn.\", \".attn.\")\n                .replace(\".weight\", \"\"))\n\n\ndef _fp8_kind(dtype):\n    s = str(dtype).lower()\n    if \"float8\" not in s:\n        return None\n    return \"e4m3\" if \"e4m3\" in s else \"e5m2\" if \"e5m2\" in s else \"unknown\"\n\n\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n#  Fused serving-weight reconstruction  (qkv / o / gateup / down)\n# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n#\n# tiered-serve serves the merged projections that vLLM builds:\n#   QKVParallelLinear     -> qkv    = cat(q_proj, k_proj, v_proj, dim=0)\n#   MergedColumnParallel  -> gateup = cat(gate_proj, up_proj,     dim=0)\n#   o_proj / down_proj stay as-is.\n# We reconstruct those from the per-projection safetensors so the benchmark\n# shapes match the production weight layout (and the _FUSED_MAX_N_TABLE tuning).\n\n_LAYER_RE = re.compile(r\"layers\\.(\\d+)\\.\")\n\n_ROLE_PATS = (\n    (\"q_proj\", \"q\"), (\"k_proj\", \"k\"), (\"v_proj\", \"v\"), (\"o_proj\", \"o\"),\n    (\"gate_proj\", \"gate\"), (\"up_proj\", \"up\"), (\"down_proj\", \"down\"),\n    (\".wq.\", \"q\"), (\".wk.\", \"k\"), (\".wv.\", \"v\"), (\".wo.\", \"o\"),\n    (\".w1.\", \"gate\"), (\".w3.\", \"up\"), (\".w2.\", \"down\"),\n)\n\n#: Fused group name -> the projection roles concatenated along dim 0.\n_GROUP_DEFS = OrderedDict([\n    (\"qkv\", (\"q\", \"k\", \"v\")),\n    (\"o\", (\"o\",)),\n    (\"gateup\", (\"gate\", \"up\")),\n    (\"down\", (\"down\",)),\n])\n\n\ndef _role(key):\n    for pat, r in _ROLE_PATS:\n        if pat in key:\n            return r\n    return None\n\n\ndef _build_layer_index(shards, layer_filter):\n    \"\"\"Map ``layer_idx -> {role: (shard_path, key)}`` across all shards.\"\"\"\n    index = {}\n    for shard in shards:\n        with safe_open(shard, framework=\"pt\") as sf:\n            for k in sf.keys():\n                r = _role(k)\n                if r is None:\n                    continue\n                m = _LAYER_RE.search(k)\n                if m is None:\n                    continue\n                li = int(m.group(1))\n                if layer_filter is not None and li != layer_filter:\n                    continue\n                index.setdefault(li, {})[r] = (shard, k)\n    return index\n\n\ndef _load_layer(parts):\n    \"\"\"Load every projection tensor for one layer; ``role -> CPU tensor``.\"\"\"\n    by_shard = {}\n    for role, (shard, key) in parts.items():\n        by_shard.setdefault(shard, []).append((role, key))\n    out = {}\n    for shard, items in by_shard.items():\n        with safe_open(shard, framework=\"pt\") as sf:\n            for role, key in items:\n                out[role] = sf.get_tensor(key)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _max_fused_numel(index, group_filter):\n    \"\"\"Largest element count among the fused groups that will be benchmarked.\n\n    Reads tensor shapes from the safetensors header (no data load) so the\n    DietGPU ANS workspace can be pre-sized to the biggest single compress\n    input — otherwise it ``cudaMalloc``s a fresh temp buffer on every call\n    for large weights (e.g. fused gateup), biasing its compress timing.\n    \"\"\"\n    by_shard = {}\n    for layer, parts in index.items():\n        for role, (shard, key) in parts.items():\n            by_shard.setdefault(shard, []).append((layer, role, key))\n    role_numel = {}  # (layer, role) -> numel\n    for shard, items in by_shard.items():\n        with safe_open(shard, framework=\"pt\") as sf:\n            for layer, role, key in items:\n                n = 1\n                for d in sf.get_slice(key).get_shape():\n                    n *= d\n                role_numel[(layer, role)] = n\n    best = 0\n    for layer in index:\n        for gname, roles in _GROUP_DEFS.items():\n            if group_filter is not None and gname not in group_filter:\n                continue\nFILE:benchmarks/fuseGEMM.py\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Unified codec decision benchmark for the tiered-serving weight path.\n\nFor each compressor codec (zipserv / p4flat / ublb_flat) and each Llama-3.1-70B\nprojection (qkv, o, gate_up, down) this measures the data needed to calibrate\nthe serving strategy, per token count N, between three choices:\n\n  1. fused             — decompress + GEMM in one kernel (no dense HBM write)\n  2. decomp-then-GEMM  — decompress to a dense bf16 weight, then cuBLAS\n  3. raw bf16 load     — skip compression, GEMM the dense bf16 weight directly\n                         (the compute floor; its load cost = raw_bytes / BW is\n                         estimated from the reported ratio)\n\nReported per (codec, proj):\n  * compress time, decompress time, compression ratio + compressed bytes\nReported per (codec, layer, proj, N), under TWO conditions — isolated and with a\nconcurrent H2D memcpy running (mimicking the next layer's weight offload):\n  * raw GEMM, decomp+GEMM, fused latency P50/P95\n\nWhy the concurrent-H2D condition: decomp-then-GEMM writes the full dense weight\nto HBM, which contends with the weight-offload H2D copy + HBM write bandwidth;\nfused has no dense write and is contention-immune. An isolated sweep therefore\nwrongly favours decomp for O/GateUp/Down — the in-engine flip the codec\nthreshold tables (P4FlatCompressor._FUSED_MAX_N_TABLE etc.) already encode.\n\nTo characterise the fused KERNEL at every N (so production thresholds can be\ncalibrated), the per-codec production N-thresholds are forced wide open.\n\nUsage:\n  PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) ./.venv/bin/python benchmark_codec_decision.py\n  ... --synthetic --check --n-values 1,64,256\n  ... --csv codec_decision.csv\n  ... --codecs zipserv,p4flat --projs o,gate_up\n  ... --ats --codecs p4flat --projs gate_up   # GH200: exp->LPDDR/C2C, mant->HBM\n\nWith ``--ats`` (GH200 only) the codec's compressed-exponent stream is relocated\nto Grace LPDDR (the raw sign|mantissa byte stream stays in HBM) and BOTH\ncompressed strategies are re-measured reading that exponent over the NVLink-C2C\nlink, adding two iso/h2d column groups:\n\n  * decmpATS  — decompress (exponent from LPDDR/C2C, mantissa from HBM) into a\n                dense bf16 weight in HBM, then cuBLAS GEMM (still an HBM write).\n  * fusedATS  — fused decode+GEMM; the exponent streams from LPDDR straight into\n                the SMs, no dense-weight HBM staging at all.\n\nThis gives the direct HBM-vs-C2C comparison for the decomp+GEMM and fused paths\nalike.  See\n``ats-benchmarks/benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py``.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport ctypes\nimport glob\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\n\n# Allow running as `python benchmarks/fuseGEMM.py ...` from the repo root (or\n# anywhere) without needing PYTHONPATH — add the repo root (parent of this\n# benchmarks/ dir) to sys.path so `import tiered_serve` resolves.\n_REPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\nif _REPO_ROOT not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, _REPO_ROOT)\n\nimport torch\n\nfrom benchmarks.fused_bench_common import (\n    H2DContender,\n    LatencyStats,\n    add_timing,\n    bench_cuda,\n    runtime_metadata,\n    sha256_file,\n    sha256_tensor,\n    write_csv,\n)\n\n# Silence per-compress codec INFO spam (logged once per timed iteration).\nlogging.getLogger(\"tiered_serve\").setLevel(logging.WARNING)\n\n\n# ── Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct projection shapes (M=out, K=in) ───────────────────\nHIDDEN_SIZE = 8192\nNUM_Q_HEADS = 64\nNUM_KV_HEADS = 8\nHEAD_DIM = 128\nINTERMEDIATE_SIZE = 28672\nN_LAYERS = 80\n\nQ_DIM = NUM_Q_HEADS * HEAD_DIM          # 8192\nKV_DIM = NUM_KV_HEADS * HEAD_DIM        # 1024\nQKV_OUT = Q_DIM + 2 * KV_DIM            # 10240\nGATEUP_OUT = 2 * INTERMEDIATE_SIZE      # 57344\n\n\ndef proj_shapes(tp):\n    \"\"\"Return {proj: (M, K)} for one decode layer under tensor-parallelism tp.\n\n    Column-parallel (qkv, gate_up) shard the output dim; row-parallel (o, down)\n    shard the contraction dim.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"qkv\":     (QKV_OUT // tp,    HIDDEN_SIZE),\n        \"o\":       (HIDDEN_SIZE,      Q_DIM // tp),\n        \"gate_up\": (GATEUP_OUT // tp, HIDDEN_SIZE),\n        \"down\":    (HIDDEN_SIZE,      INTERMEDIATE_SIZE // tp),\n    }\n\n\n# ── Timing helpers (mirror benchmark_decode_gemm.py conventions) ─────────────\n_L2_FLUSH_SIZE = 128 * 1024 * 1024  # bytes; > GH200 L2 to guarantee a flush\n_l2_flush_buf = None\n\n\ndef flush_l2_cache():\n    global _l2_flush_buf\n    if _l2_flush_buf is None:\n        _l2_flush_buf = torch.empty(_L2_FLUSH_SIZE // 4, dtype=torch.float32,\n                                    device=\"cuda\")\n    _l2_flush_buf.zero_()\n\n\ndef bench_gpu_stats(fn, warmup, iters, flush) -> LatencyStats:\n    \"\"\"P50/P95 per-iteration GPU time in an isolated stream.\"\"\"\n    return bench_cuda(\n        fn, warmup, iters,\n        flush_fn=flush_l2_cache if flush else None,\n    )\n\n\ndef bench_gpu(fn, warmup, iters, flush):\n    \"\"\"Backward-compatible P50-only wrapper used by older imports.\"\"\"\n    return bench_gpu_stats(fn, warmup, iters, flush).p50_ms\n\n\ndef bench_compute_stats(fn, warmup, iters, flush, contender=None,\n                        copies_per_iter=8) -> LatencyStats:\n    return bench_cuda(\n        fn, warmup, iters,\n        flush_fn=flush_l2_cache if flush else None,\n        contender=contender,\n        copies_per_iter=copies_per_iter,\n    )\n\n\ndef bench_compute(fn, warmup, iters, flush, contender=None, copies_per_iter=8):\n    \"\"\"Backward-compatible P50-only wrapper used by older scripts.\"\"\"\n    return bench_compute_stats(\n        fn, warmup, iters, flush, contender, copies_per_iter).p50_ms\n\n\n# ── Weight sources ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nDEFAULT_WEIGHTS_DIR = (\n    \"/root/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--meta-llama--Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct\"\n    \"/snapshots/1605565b47bb9346c5515c34102e054115b4f98b\"\n)\n\n\ndef _layer_idx(name):\n    m = re.search(r'\\.layers\\.(\\d+)\\.', name)\n    return int(m.group(1)) if m else None\n\n\ndef load_real_projections(weights_dir, want_shapes, max_shards=6, layer=None):\n    \"\"\"Return {proj: bf16 CPU tensor (M,K)} pulled from real Llama-70B weights.\n\n    Fuses q+k+v -> qkv and gate+up -> gate_up per layer, then takes the first\n    tensor whose shape matches each requested projection.  Reads shards until\n    every wanted shape is satisfied.\n\n    ``layer`` (int) restricts the scan to that decoder layer's weights — use it\n    to pin the measurement to a representative layer (e.g. the median-exception\n    layer 40) instead of whatever shard 0 happens to expose first (layer 0, the\n    314k-exception QKV outlier).  All shards are scanned when ``layer`` is set,\n    since a high layer can live past ``max_shards``.\n    \"\"\"\n    from safetensors import safe_open\n    files = so