{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T07:59:29.207Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03d14-cfb7-73f0-8f27-25827d8684ef","call_id":"call_DocRyx34wzGhdzogwpeGhvCD","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"BRANCHES\n* main                              0d818c0 [origin/main: ahead 1] Validate explicit dedicated KV block configuration\n  refactor/split-dual-memory-loader 1d41e25 Increase look-ahead depth for frozen-split\n  remotes/origin/HEAD               -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/eurosys-fall       2c9a993 Merge pull request #1 from Sys-KU/main\n  remotes/origin/main               bcb619e Fix auto weight compressor family lookup\n  remotes/quiverdance/main          0d818c0 Validate explicit dedicated KV block configuration\nBENCH COMMITS\neee385dd55d5d0da6a8ab92ae9bf5271699fc3f3\nba785729cfd6d2e0b64edfe4c90d0d7d5555bd50\n2026-06-18 12:01:39 +0900\nBulk update\n6faee06c1c9b7f81f19439ab2259d15fedeb831e\ne92bb9f59534f7ea668c4f05c82dddfc5ec45446\n2026-06-19 02:25:19 +0900\nAdd ats path\ncad11aec158adda0fbe343ceb89893c2da783d02\ne49cb4f4f3b929035b6bab3baf3f124e310d1b50\n2026-08-06 19:38:05 +0900\nConsolidate weight and KV offload correctness\nATS README\n# Compression Benchmarks\n\nThis directory contains GPU compression and ATS/direct-host-access benchmarks\nfor BF16 KV blocks and model weights.\n\nThe C++/CUDA binaries focus on nvCOMP Bitcomp host-compression paths.  The\nPython benchmarks compare H2D+decompress, ATS-direct decompression, ZipServ,\nDietGPU, and CPU zstd mantissa decompression paths.\n\nRun commands from the repository root:\n\n```bash\ncd /root/projects/ats-benchmarks\n```\n\nUse the `tiered-serve` Python environment for Python benchmarks:\n\n```bash\nPY=/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/bin/python\n```\n\n## Build\n\nBuild the compression binaries:\n\n```bash\nmake bitcomp\nmake bitcomp_omp\n```\n\nOr build every compression binary:\n\n```bash\nmake compress\n```\n\nThe Python benchmarks JIT-build their required PyTorch CUDA extensions on first\nrun.  They expect the sibling repositories and libraries referenced by the\nscripts to be available, including `tiered-serve`, `LLM-bitfield-compressor`,\nCUDA, nvCOMP, and DietGPU/ZipServ dependencies for the selected codec.\n\n## Native Bitcomp Benchmarks\n\nSingle-path Bitcomp benchmark:\n\n```bash\n./bin/bitcomp --chunks 8192 --chunk-bytes 32768 --iters 1 --verify 1\n```\n\nOpenMP copy-vs-ATS Bitcomp benchmark:\n\n```bash\n./bin/bitcomp_omp \\\n  --chunks 8192 \\\n  --chunk-bytes 32768 \\\n  --pattern random \\\n  --iters 1 \\\n  --verify 1\n```\n\nOptional OpenMP thread pinning:\n\n```bash\nexport OMP_NUM_THREADS=16\nexport OMP_DYNAMIC=false\nexport OMP_PROC_BIND=true\nexport OMP_PLACES=cores\n```\n\n## nvCOMP H2D vs ATS\n\n`python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py` compares compressed BF16 data copied to HBM before\ndecompression against compressed data read directly from registered hugepage host\nmemory through ATS.  It also reports SM-copy bandwidth from host memory to HBM.\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py \\\n  --codec ans bitcomp zipserv \\\n  --size-mib 64\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --block-sweep 1 16 256 4096\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py \\\n  --codec zipserv \\\n  --use-kv-cache\n```\n\nSupported codecs are `gdeflate`, `zstd`, `bitcomp`, `lz4`, `ans`, and\n`zipserv`.  The default generated block shape is `128x128` BF16, or 32 KiB per\nblock.\n\n## BF16 Split Exp/Sign-Mantissa ATS\n\n`python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py` benchmarks split-stream BF16\nreconstruct/decompress latency with compressed exponent and sign-mantissa\nstreams placed in HBM or LPDDR/ATS-backed hugepage memory.  It supports\ngenerated BF16 blocks, `kv_blocks_cache.pt` inputs, and `.safetensors` or `.pt`\nweight inputs.  It prints HBM, Exp-in-ATS, and Exp+sign_mantissa-in-ATS rows.\n\nGenerated data:\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  --codec dietgpu \\\n  --size-mib 256\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  --codec zipserv \\\n  --size-mib 256\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --size-mib 256\n```\n\nFile inputs:\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  benchmarks/compress/kv_blocks_cache.pt \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --max-tensors 256\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model-00001-of-00030.safetensors \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --layer 0 \\\n  --max-tensors 128\n```\n\nOptional placement sanity check:\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  benchmarks/compress/kv_blocks_cache.pt \\\n  --codec zipserv \\\n  --max-tensors 4096 \\\n  --measure-exp-copy\n```\n\n`Write GB/s` is decompressed BF16 output write throughput.  `Read GB/s` counts\nthe compressed/reconstruct input streams read by the timed path.  `LPDDR GB/s`\ncounts only the streams placed in LPDDR for that row: Exp for the `Exp` row,\nand Exp+sign_mantissa for the `Exp+SM` row.  If HBM and ATS decompress latency\nare close, use `--measure-exp-copy` to measure the Exp stream by itself and\nconfirm the HBM-vs-ATS bandwidth gap.\n\nFor ZipServ, the default `--zipserv-api pure` path precomputes output pointers\nand `start_exp` on GPU before timing, so the measured HBM row does not include\nthe legacy binding's per-call control H2D copies.  Use `--zipserv-api legacy`\nonly when intentionally timing the original Python binding path.\n\nFor DietGPU, the default `--dietgpu-api pure` path precomputes pointer and\ncapacity arrays on GPU before timing, so the measured HBM row does not include\nDietGPU's per-call pointer-array H2D copies.  `--dietgpu-api inline128` is a\nfallback that avoids those copies by using DietGPU's <=128-block inline-provider\npath, and `--dietgpu-api legacy` times the original single-call binding.\n\n## zstd Mantissa ATS\n\n`python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py` compresses BF16 mantissa tiles with zstd, then\ncompares CPU decompression through a DMA path against CPU direct C2C access to\nGPU HBM on GH200-style systems.\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model-00001-of-00030.safetensors\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model-00001-of-00030.safetensors \\\n  --tile 512 \\\n  --workers 64 \\\n  --layer 0 \\\n  --max-weights 7\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model.pt \\\n  --all-weights \\\n  --max-weights 16\n```\n\n## ATS and Hugepages\n\nThe ATS benchmarks use hugepage-backed host memory by default:\n\n```bash\n--hugepage-dir /mnt/hugepages\n```\n\nMake sure that directory is mounted and has enough free hugepage capacity for\nthe selected data size.  Use smaller `--size-mib`, `--num-blocks`, or\n`--max-tensors` values when doing quick smoke tests or when hugepage memory is\nlimited.\nATS BENCH HEADERS\nFILE:/root/projects/ats-benchmarks/benchmarks/compress/bench_cpu_encode_compare.py\n\"\"\"Fair CPU-encode throughput: ublb_tbe (C++ OpenMP) vs p4flatcpu, real KV.\n\nBoth are the production C++ OpenMP host encoders, measured as ONE call over N\nstacked KV blocks at the current OMP_NUM_THREADS (so the comparison is the raw\nencoder, not Python/ThreadPool plumbing):\n\n  * ublb_tbe : ublb_tbe_ext.tbe_host_encode(w_u16)         (NEW)\n  * p4flat   : zipserv_p4flat_ext.host_encode_blocks(...)  (the p4flatcpu path)\n\nSet the thread count via OMP_NUM_THREADS (sweep by re-running). Run from\ntiered-serve:\n  for T in 1 8 32; do OMP_NUM_THREADS=$T PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) ./.venv/bin/python \\\\\n    /root/projects/ats-benchmarks/benchmarks/compress/bench_cpu_encode_compare.py; done\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport time\n\nimport torch\n\nPATH = \"/root/projects/ats-benchmarks/benchmarks/compress/kv_blocks_cache.pt\"\nMB = KB = 128                      # KV block reshaped to [128,128]\nRAW_PER_BLOCK = MB * KB * 2\n\n\ndef _best(fn, warmup=3, iters=10):\n    for _ in range(warmup):\n        fn()\n    best = 1e30\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        fn()\n        best = min(best, time.perf_counter() - t0)\n    return best\n\n\ndef main():\n    N = int(os.environ.get(\"NBLK\", \"512\"))\n    omp = os.environ.get(\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\", \"all\")\n    obj = torch.load(PATH, map_location=\"cpu\", weights_only=False)\n    blocks = {\n        \"K\": [obj[\"k_blocks\"][i].contiguous().reshape(MB, KB) for i in range(N)],\n        \"V\": [obj[\"v_blocks\"][i].contiguous().reshape(MB, KB) for i in range(N)],\n    }\n    raw = N * RAW_PER_BLOCK\n    gib = lambda s: raw / s / 1024**3\n    print(f\"real KV: N={N}/side  block=[{MB}x{KB}]  raw/side={raw/1024**2:.1f} MiB  \"\n          f\"OMP_NUM_THREADS={omp}\")\n\n    from tiered_serve.compression.core.ublb_tbe import _get_ext as _ublb_ext\n    uext = _ublb_ext()\n    from tiered_serve.cpp_exts import zipserv_p4flat_ext as pext\n    has_p4 = hasattr(pext, \"host_encode_blocks\")\n\n    print(f\"\\n  {'codec':<16} {'side':<4} {'ratio':>6} {'GiB/s':>8} {'us/blk':>8}\")\n    print(\"  \" + \"─\" * 46)\n    for side, bl in blocks.items():\n        # ── ublb_tbe C++ ──\n        stack = torch.cat(bl, 0).contiguous()\n        wu = stack.view(torch.uint16).reshape(-1).contiguous()\n        outs = uext.tbe_host_encode(wu)\n        ubytes = sum(t.numel() * t.element_size() for t in outs)\n        t = _best(lambda: uext.tbe_host_encode(wu))\n        print(f\"  {'ublb_tbe(C++)':<16} {side:<4} {raw/ubytes:>5.3f}x \"\n              f\"{gib(t):>8.2f} {t/N*1e6:>8.2f}\")\n\n        # ── ublb_flat C++ (flat 4-bit palette, simpler -> faster encode) ──\n        if hasattr(uext, \"flat_host_encode\"):\n            fouts = uext.flat_host_encode(wu)\n            fbytes = sum(t.numel() * t.element_size() for t in fouts)\n            t = _best(lambda: uext.flat_host_encode(wu))\n            print(f\"  {'ublb_flat(C++)':<16} {side:<4} {raw/fbytes:>5.3f}x \"\n                  f\"{gib(t):>8.2f} {t/N*1e6:>8.2f}\")\n\n        # ── p4flat C++ (host_encode_blocks = p4flatcpu) ──\n        if has_p4:\n            src = torch.stack(bl).view(torch.int16).contiguous()   # [N,128,128]\n            host_n = N + 1\n            max_comp = 32768\n            blob = torch.empty(host_n, max_comp, dtype=torch.uint8)\n            tot = torch.zeros(host_n, dtype=torch.int32)\n            ec = torch.zeros(host_n, dtype=torch.int32)\n            israw = torch.zeros(host_n, dtype=torch.uint8)\n            vr = torch.zeros(host_n, dtype=torch.int32)\n            bid = torch.arange(N, dtype=torch.long)\n            slots = torch.arange(N, dtype=torch.long)\n            valid_tm = MB // 64\n\n            def run_p4():\n                pext.host_encode_blocks(src, bid, slots, blob, tot, ec, israw,\n                                        vr, MB, KB, valid_tm)\n            run_p4()\n            pbytes = int(tot[:N].sum().item())\n            t = _best(run_p4)\n            print(f\"  {'p4flat(C++)':<16} {side:<4} {raw/pbytes:>5.3f}x \"\n                  f\"{gib(t):>8.2f} {t/N*1e6:>8.2f}\")\n\n    print(\"\\n  (one C++ call over N stacked blocks at OMP_NUM_THREADS.)\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\nFILE:/root/projects/ats-benchmarks/benchmarks/compress/bench_kv_compress_latency.py\n\"\"\"Cross-codec GPU KV-block compress/decode latency on a real KV dump.\n\nAnswers: \"for each codec, how long does it take to compress one KV cache block\non the GPU (and decode it back)?\" — apples-to-apples, per-block, on the real\n``kv_blocks_cache.pt`` dump, for K and V separately (their distributions, hence\nratio and out-of-palette rates, differ).\n\nCodecs (all expose a per-tensor ``.compress([M,K]) / .decompress``):\n\n  * ublb_tbe : UBLBTBECompressor — UB/LB byte split, upper-byte triple-bitmap\n              